---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support SecArsenal"
  description="SecArsenal carries no ads and no sponsor placements. Optional, transparent, recurring support goes through Open Collective, where every dollar in and out is public."
>
  <div>
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Support' }]} />
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">Support SecArsenal</h1>

    <section class="mt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">No ads, no sponsors</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
        SecArsenal doesn't run ads, sponsor placements, or paid listings —
        no tool or distro on this site got here, or got ranked, because
        someone paid for it. That's a deliberate choice: this is a
        reference catalog, and a reference is only useful if its
        selection can't be bought. Real costs still exist, though —
        hosting, the domain, and the public MCP server (see
        <a class="text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300" href="https://github.com/brando5393/secarsenal/blob/master/mcp-server/README.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">mcp-server ↗</a>) —
        and covering those with visible, optional community support beats
        quietly adding the kind of monetization this page just ruled out.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Why Open Collective</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
        Recurring support runs through
        <a class="text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300" href="https://opencollective.com/secarsenal" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Open Collective ↗</a>,
        not Patreon or a similar platform. Open Collective's whole model is
        a public ledger — every contribution in and every expense out is
        visible on the collective's page, not just a total. For a project
        that indexes penetration-testing tools, that transparency matters
        more than convenience: "publicly funded, dollar-for-dollar
        visible" is a stronger, more legitimate footing than an opaque
        tip jar.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4">
        <a
          class="inline-block rounded-md bg-emerald-500 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-950 no-underline transition-colors hover:bg-emerald-400"
          href="https://opencollective.com/secarsenal"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
        >
          Open the collective ↗
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Other ways to help</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
        Money isn't the only useful contribution. Fixing a stale link,
        adding a missing logo, or writing up a new OS/tool entry is worth
        at least as much — see
        <a class="text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300" href="https://github.com/brando5393/secarsenal/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">CONTRIBUTING.md ↗</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
